# Build-time configuration for the hosted PWA.
#
# These are NOT secrets. Vite inlines every VITE_* value into the client
# bundle, so the anon key is already sitting inside every build this project
# has ever produced, and inside the Android APK. Row Level Security is what
# protects the data behind it -- and as of 2026-09-11 that is actually true:
# the two holes the anon key could reach (INSERT on `signals`, EXECUTE on
# trigger_auto_execute) were closed in
# 20260911195543_harden_signals_rls_and_executor_grants.
#
# Committed deliberately, forced past the root .gitignore's `.env.*` rule.
# Without it a clean clone -- or a git-linked Vercel build -- passes
# `vite build` and then throws at runtime in supabaseClient.ts, which means a
# deployment that reports success and serves a white screen. The failure is
# silent, so the fix belongs in the repo rather than in one dashboard.
#
# The service-role key is NOT here and must never be. If a value ever needs to
# stay secret, it does not belong in a VITE_ variable at all -- it belongs
# behind an edge function.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://epulmnfbxjmaimefhofp.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImVwdWxtbmZieGptYWltZWZob2ZwIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3NzYwMTE4NDMsImV4cCI6MjA5MTU4Nzg0M30.zb5mEF5YKu80lZ_moQcxcqT43FkS4XYEjuF6cEnSy5k
